<header class="top">
  <div class="top-inner">
    <div class="title-row">
      <img class="project-mark" src="assets/field-ledger-mark.svg" alt="">
      <h1>Columbus Micromobility — Observer View</h1>
      <span class="badge">Independent observer · public data only</span>
    </div>
    <p class="desc">An independent, public-data-only look at Columbus shared-scooter operations — 311 requests, published vehicle positions, and policy boundaries. Built from public sources only; not affiliated with or using data from any employer.</p>
    <div class="caveat">
      <strong>Partial sample snapshot.</strong> The data embedded below was extracted from a size-capped fetch of
      <a href="https://github.com/steveneedham/311-Intel" target="_blank" rel="noopener">github.com/steveneedham/311-Intel</a>'s
      public data feeds and is <strong>not the full dataset</strong> — see per-layer counts in the stat cards and the
      <code>_extraction_note</code> embedded in each JSON block below. This is a review signal for demo purposes, not a confirmed
      or complete picture of citywide activity. To see the full dataset, swap in the complete committed JSON files
      (<code>columbus-311-current.json</code>, <code>gbfs-vehicle-positions.json</code>, <code>mobility-policy-boundaries.json</code>)
      from that repo. This dashboard itself is destined for
      <a href="https://github.com/steveneedham/columbus-micromobility-data" target="_blank" rel="noopener">github.com/steveneedham/columbus-micromobility-data</a>.
      Not an official Spin, Veo, or City of Columbus tool — not a confirmed-violation record system.
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<main>
  <div class="stat-grid" id="statGrid"></div>

  <div class="layout">
    <div class="panel">
      <div class="panel-header">Map — source-labeled, public-data only</div>
      <div id="map"></div>
    </div>

    <div class="sidebar">
      <div class="panel controls">
        <div class="panel-header" style="margin: -14px -16px 4px;">Layers &amp; filters</div>
        <label><input type="checkbox" id="toggle311" checked> 311 requests (review signal, not confirmed violations)</label>
        <label><input type="checkbox" id="toggleGbfs" checked> GBFS vehicle positions</label>
        <label><input type="checkbox" id="togglePileups" checked> Cross-vendor flags</label>
        <label><input type="checkbox" id="togglePolicy" checked> Policy boundaries</label>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="operatorFilter">Operator</label>
          <select id="operatorFilter">
            <option value="all">All</option>
            <option value="Veo">Veo</option>
            <option value="Spin">Spin</option>
          </select>
        </div>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="availFilter">Availability</label>
          <select id="availFilter">
            <option value="all">All</option>
            <option value="available">Available</option>
            <option value="unavailable">Unavailable</option>
          </select>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="panel legend">
        <div class="panel-header" style="margin: -12px -16px 8px;">Legend</div>
        <div class="legend-row"><span class="swatch" style="background:#dc2626;"></span> 311 — critical (ADA ramp/entrance)</div>
        <div class="legend-row"><span class="swatch" style="background:#f97316;"></span> 311 — high (ADA concern / sidewalk pile)</div>
        <div class="legend-row"><span class="swatch" style="background:#64748b;"></span> 311 — standard</div>
        <div class="legend-row"><span class="swatch" style="background:#0d9488;"></span> GBFS — Veo</div>
        <div class="legend-row"><span class="swatch" style="background:#f97316;"></span> GBFS — Spin</div>
        <div class="legend-row"><span class="swatch ring"></span> Cross-vendor pile-up flag</div>
        <div class="legend-row"><span class="swatch line"></span> Policy boundary</div>
      </div>

      <div class="panel">
        <div class="panel-header">Cross-vendor pile-ups</div>
        <div class="pileup-list" id="pileupList"></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="reference-library" aria-labelledby="reference-library-title">
    <p class="eyebrow">Reference artifacts · July 2026</p>
    <h2 id="reference-library-title">Forecast source guides and inventories</h2>
    <p class="reference-intro">Downloadable working artifacts document the event, home-game, ISO-week, and weather context used for demand planning. The ChatGPT and Claude files are retained as separate reference sets so their provenance remains visible.</p>

    <div class="reference-grid">
      <article class="reference-item">
        <div class="reference-label">ChatGPT · Field Ledger edition</div>
        <h3>ChatGPT Forecast</h3>
        <p>Branded operating guide with event and game separation, ISO-week correlation, historical weather, projected weather-risk caveats, and source methodology.</p>
        <div class="reference-links">
          <a href="ChatGPT%20Forecast.docx" download>Word guide</a>
          <a href="ChatGPT%20Forecast.xlsx" download>Excel inventory</a>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="reference-item">
        <div class="reference-label">Claude · Reference edition</div>
        <h3>Claude Forecast</h3>
        <p>Companion source guide and historical event workbook retained as supplied for comparison and reference.</p>
        <div class="reference-links">
          <a href="Claude%20Forecast%20-%20Columbus_Micromobility_Event_Demand_Sources_branded.docx" download>Word guide</a>
          <a href="Claude%20Forecast%200%20Columbus_Micromobility_Events_Historical_2024-2026.xlsx" download>Excel inventory</a>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>

    <div class="forecast-visuals" aria-label="ChatGPT Forecast visual references">
      <figure class="forecast-visual">
        <img src="demand-forecast-card.svg" alt="ChatGPT Forecast project card summarizing canonical events, home games, weather-risk days, and the ISO-week join">
        <figcaption>Project card · <a href="demand-forecast-card.svg">SVG</a> · <a href="demand-forecast-card.png">PNG</a></figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="forecast-visual">
        <img src="demand-forecast-chart.svg" alt="Illustrative weekly demand signals chart with separate major-event, home-game, and weather-risk layers">
        <figcaption>Illustrative chart · not model output · <a href="demand-forecast-chart.svg">SVG</a> · <a href="demand-forecast-chart.png">PNG</a></figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>

<footer>© 2026 Steven Needham · Independent project, public data only.</footer>

